{"title":"Career Roadmap · Veterinary Doctor","role":"Veterinary Doctor","summary":"A Veterinary Doctor is a qualified animal-health professional responsible for the prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and management of diseases and injuries in animals.","facts":{"Current degree":"BVSc & AH (Veterinary Science & Animal Husbandry)","Course":"Veterinary Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Veterinary Doctor is a qualified animal-health professional responsible for the prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and management of diseases and injuries in animals."},{"type":"h","text":"Veterinarians may work with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Companion animals such as dogs and cats"},{"type":"h","text":"Livestock such as cattle, buffaloes, sheep, goats, and pigs"},{"type":"h","text":"Poultry"},{"type":"h","text":"Horses and other working animals"},{"type":"h","text":"Wildlife"},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory animals"},{"type":"h","text":"Aquatic and aquatic-associated species, depending on specialization"},{"type":"p","text":"The profession also contributes to food safety, zoonotic disease control, animal production, public health, vaccination programmes, disease surveillance, and animal welfare."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"10+2 / Intermediate"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Physics"},{"type":"h","text":"├── Chemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"└── Biology"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"NEET-UG / Applicable"},{"type":"h","text":"Veterinary Admission Route"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"BVSc & AH"},{"type":"h","text":"Veterinary Science &"},{"type":"h","text":"Animal Husbandry"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Training /"},{"type":"h","text":"Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"│"},{"type":"h","text":"▼"},{"type":"